They reflected that a morning walk is good exercise and that an early riser can be a regular morning walker, with manifold benefits. In the early morning everything looks fresh and fair, the atmosphere is pleasant and calm, and a morning walker breathes pollution-free air while enjoying the lovely sights and sounds of nature, all of which soothes the soul. They noted that a regular morning walk keeps one fit and helps build sound health; science says it controls blood pressure, lessens stress and strain, and energizes one to work zealously. They observed that nowadays we live a very fast life and work around the clock, hardly finding time to care for our health, but if the habit of a morning walk is formed from an early age, one can be sure of a sound body and a sound mind. Besides the health benefits, they find it an extremely delightful experience to take a walk early in the morning.